     "type": "text",
     "text": "{\"reachable\": false, \"rationale\": \"With mfa_admin deployed, the attacker cannot reach data exfiltration. The attacker gets far into the network but is stopped at the domain controller. Reachable steps: phish_workstation gives foothold_workstation and stolen_user. pivot_internal works because segmented is false, giving reach_internal. auth_appserver works because mfa_user is false, giving foothold_appserver. kerberoast_dc then gives stolen_admin, and escalate_appserver gives admin_appserver. The blocked step: auth_dc requires NOT mfa_admin, so foothold_dc is never achieved. That means escalate_dc cannot fire, so admin_dc stays false, and dump_dbadmin_dc cannot fire, so stolen_dbadmin stays false. Consequence: dump_dbadmin_dc is the only source of stolen_dbadmin, and auth_db and auth_fileserver both require it. So foothold_db and foothold_fileserver are unreachable, which keeps admin_db and admin_fileserver false. Both exfiltration techniques (exfiltrate_db and exfiltrate_fileserver) need one of those, so exfiltrated cannot become true.\"}"
    }
   ],
